@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-eu`

-- Tests for uk-interpretation-eu.l4. Each expected value was decided by reading the section and written down before the module was run.
-- The days the Act refers to without giving are INPUTS. Here "IP completion day" is 31 December 2020 and section 20A is taken to have come into force on
-- 1 January 2021; both are illustrations that the tests pick, and are not claims about the Acts that give those days.

§ `Section 20(2A)`

-- all of (a) and (b) met, required: the reference is to the document as it so has effect
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `as it so has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
-- "including, so far as so required, as it has effect from time to time"
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as it so has effect, including as it has effect from time to time`
-- the Act is passed "on or after IP completion day": the day itself is in, the day before is out
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `as it so has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2020 12 30) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- each of the conditions is needed
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- "unless the contrary intention appears"
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- "so far as required for the purposes of relevant separation agreement law"
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
#ASSERT `section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`

§ `Section 20(3) and (4)`

#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `an EU regulation` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `an EU decision` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `EU tertiary legislation` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `a provision of the EEA agreement` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `something else` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- "passed on or after IP completion day"
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) `an EU regulation` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2020 12 30) (YMD 2020 12 31) `an EU regulation` FALSE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- "unless the contrary intention appears"
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `an EU regulation` TRUE `no reading is given by this provision` EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- "Subject to subsection (2A)": where (2A) gives a reading, that reading stands
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `an EU regulation` FALSE `as it so has effect, including as it has effect from time to time` EQUALS `as it so has effect, including as it has effect from time to time`
#ASSERT `section 20(3) — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) `something else` FALSE `as it so has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018` EQUALS `as it so has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
-- subsection (4)
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(4) provides that subsection (3) determines whether the reference is read as a reference to the thing as modified by domestic law`
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 20(4) — whether the reference is read as a reference to the thing as modified by domestic law` TRUE BECAUSE "section 20(4) leaves open whether the reference is to the document as modified by domestic law, and the sources do not answer it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 20(4) — whether the reference is read as a reference to the thing as modified by domestic law` FALSE BECAUSE "section 20(4) says nothing about a reference to which subsection (3) does not apply"

§ `Section 20(5) and (6)`

#ASSERT `section 20(5) — the meaning of the expression in subsections (2A) to (4)` TRUE (JUST "the meaning in that Act") EQUALS (JUST "the meaning in that Act")
#ASSERT `section 20(5) — the meaning of the expression in subsections (2A) to (4)` FALSE (JUST "the meaning in that Act") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 20(5) — the meaning of the expression in subsections (2A) to (4)` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 20(5) — the meaning of the expression in subsections (2A) to (4)` TRUE NOTHING BECAUSE "section 20(5) takes the meaning from the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it"
#ASSERT `section 20(6) counts the thing as a treaty` `a treaty`
#ASSERT `section 20(6) counts the thing as a treaty` `an international agreement`
#ASSERT `section 20(6) counts the thing as a treaty` `a protocol to a treaty or international agreement`
#ASSERT `section 20(6) counts the thing as a treaty` `an annex to a treaty or international agreement`
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(6) counts the thing as a treaty` `something else`

§ `Section 20A`

#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `as so amended, extended or applied`
-- "passed after the commencement of this section": the section is in force from the beginning of its day
#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `as so amended, extended or applied`
#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
-- an "EU instrument" is issued by an EU institution and is not assimilated direct legislation (Schedule 1)
#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`
#ASSERT `section 20A — how the reference is read` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`

§ `Section 22(1): the carve-out`

-- before the commencement: Part I of Schedule 2 lists none of them (fork F15)
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(2A)` (YMD 1978 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20A` (YMD 1978 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(3)` (YMD 1800 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
-- after the commencement and before IP completion day: section 20(2A) to (6) are cut down by the provision they make
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(2A)` (YMD 2000 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(3)` (YMD 2020 12 30) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(4)` (YMD 2020 12 30) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(5)` (YMD 2020 12 30) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(6)` (YMD 2020 12 30) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
-- on or after IP completion day
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(2A)` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(3)` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(4)` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(5)` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(6)` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(3)` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(4)` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(5)` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20(6)` (YMD 2021 6 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- section 20A: after its own commencement
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20A` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20A` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 20A` (YMD 2030 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
